        "original_id": "4f2e71b9-129d-5cc5-b13a-de865797e2c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: “God Save the Queen”, “God Save the King”\n- Places: Commonwealth realms, British Crown Dependencies, Lancaster\n- Roles: reigning monarch, Duke of Lancaster\n- Topics: national anthem, royal anthem, lyrics changes\n\nFacts:\n- “God Save the Queen”, alternatively “God Save the King” depending on the gender of the reigning monarch, is the national or royal anthem in a number of Commonwealth realms, their territories, and the British Crown Dependencies.\n- The anthem uses the same lyrics and instrumental tune in the referenced variant, but changes the second line from “Long live our noble Queen” to “Long live our noble Duke” out of respect to the reigning monarch in their capacity as the Duke of Lancaster.",
